{"hw":"ἐράω1","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἐράω1</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἐράω</span> (A), used in <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Act.</span> </span> only in <span class=\"lex-gram\">pres.</span> and <span class=\"lex-gram\">impf.</span> (which in Poetry are <span class=\"gk\">ἔραμαι, ἠράμην</span>), <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Ion.</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἐρέω</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Archil.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">25.3</span> </span>: <span class=\"lex-gram\">impf.</span> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἤρων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.108</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">161</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ach.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">146</span> </span>:—<span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Pass.</span> </span>, <span class=\"gk\">ἀντ-ερᾶται</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Smp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">8.3</span> </span>; opt. <span class=\"gk\">ἐρῷο</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hier.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">11.11</span> </span>; <span class=\"lex-gram\">inf.</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἐρᾶσθαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Plu.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Brut.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">29</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"lex-gram\">part.</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἐρώμενος</span> (v. infr.):— also <span class=